{"id": "EUVD-2026-96923", "enisaUuid": "2accc7d3-e23b-331e-a901-82b0f47943cb", "description": "Easy!Appointments through 1.6.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in Booking::register() that allows unauthenticated attackers to modify any appointment by supplying an appointment id without its hash. Attackers can enumerate sequential appointment ids with a self-asserted manage_mode flag to rewrite appointment details, rebind them to attacker-controlled customers, and obtain management hashes for rescheduling or cancellation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T20:01:31", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/easyappointments-booking-register-appointment-takeover", "https://github.com/alextselegidis/easyappointments/blob/4bc7ecd51f3dade8e041558f2c23dda65bd6c43e/application/controllers/Booking.php#L368-L587", "https://github.com/alextselegidis/easyappointments/commit/09c6fb30b6aac0830a820d6bec3d2eb241daf150", "https://github.com/alextselegidis/easyappointments", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/easy-appointments-through-1.6.0-authorization-bypass-via-booking-register-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q8ph-7hq3-m5wq", "CVE-2026-108758"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5a8dfca8-8189-3a18-b7a0-08de3643c9ff", "product": {"name": "easyappointments", "vendor": {"name": "alextselegidis"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4bad33a4-7ec7-315e-9250-6368089ca576", "vendor": {"name": "alextselegidis"}}], "isExploited": false}